  "summary": "GroundPeony (UNC3347) is a China-nexus APT active since at least 2021, targeting government, research and telecom organizations in Taiwan and Nepal through spear-phishing and compromised legitimate websites. Its March 2023 chain delivers a ZIP containing fake update EXEs that stage mic.exe alongside a sideloaded version.dll, which decrypts mic.doc/mic.ver and runs the micDown shellcode downloader beamed at a C2 host/port stored in its config. The group was the earliest known exploiter of CVE-2022-30190 (Follina), using it during the vulnerability's zero-day window.",
  "mitre_techniques": [
    "T1566.001",
    "T1203",
    "T1574.002",
    "T1027",
    "T1584.006"
  ],
